<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Test-host environment, applied by `dotnet test` through RunSettingsFilePath in the .csproj.

     ANCHOR_TLC_JAVA_OPTS is read by translator.run_tlc and by TLCProcess, and is EMPTY for anyone
     running Anchor by hand. `-XX:TieredStopAtLevel=1` stops the JVM's C2 optimising compiler.
     Measured on this suite's models — around 40 states, under two seconds of which most is JVM
     startup:

         one run,     40 states      1.90s -> 1.59s    16% faster
         eight at once, 40 states    8.92s -> 4.68s    1.9x faster
         one run,    960k states     3.72s -> 4.00s     8% SLOWER
         one run,    6.7M states    12.17s -> 18.67s   53% SLOWER

     The win is the compiler threads that never start, not the compilation skipped: the suite runs
     many model checks at once on four physical cores, and each JVM was spending cores optimising
     code it finishes before benefiting from. The last row is why this belongs to the test host
     and not to the checker — a person's own policy might be the big model, and that is the run
     where losing C2 costs most.

     Set here rather than in a base class because it is a property of how the tests are RUN, not of
     what they test. -->
<RunSettings>
  <RunConfiguration>
    <EnvironmentVariables>
      <ANCHOR_TLC_JAVA_OPTS>-XX:TieredStopAtLevel=1</ANCHOR_TLC_JAVA_OPTS>
    </EnvironmentVariables>
  </RunConfiguration>
</RunSettings>
